 {"id":"fabro-e4ac","title":"engine: verbose tool-argument validation errors — name the failing field and expected shape","status":"open","type":"feature","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-05T16:38:13.397Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-05T16:38:13.397Z","description":"Tool argument validation errors currently surface the raw JSON-schema verdict ('is not valid under any of the schemas listed in the anyOf keyword') with no field name and no expected shape. LLM agents retry blind: 5 identical failed retries in conductor run 01M1S6MSV4's develop leg (2026-09-05) where the agent nested the workflow_source object inside workflow. Wanted: validation failures for tool arguments include (a) the failing property path, (b) the closest expected schema variant or a one-line shape hint. Complements the prompt-side schema discipline note (commit 51b2f81fc). Basis: run 01M1S6MSV4 events.","labels":["engine","agent"]}
 {"id":"fabro-571e","title":"engine: fabro_run_wait blocking tool — wait for a child run's terminal state without agent-side sleep loops","status":"open","type":"feature","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-05T16:48:27.981Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-05T16:48:27.981Z","description":"The conductor's legs currently poll child runs with agent-chosen shell sleep loops (observed: a self-chosen 300s timer in run 01M1S6MSV4's develop leg, 2026-09-05) — either wasting wall-clock when the child finishes early or burning LLM turns on frequent polls; the agent owns timing it cannot know. Wanted: a blocking fabro_run_wait tool {run_id, timeout_ms} mirroring the host-side CLI 'fabro wait': the backend polls/subscribes internally and returns the final status+reason (+PR link) only at terminal state or timeout. One call replaces the whole sleep/poll/turn cycle, reacts in seconds, and makes orchestration prompts trivial ('create, then wait'). Reuses the CLI wait semantics; SSE subscription could make it fully event-driven. Basis: conductor pass 01M1S6MSV4 develop leg events.","labels":["engine","workflows","agent"]}
 {"id":"fabro-94e8","title":"engine: run-branch PRs go stale when the base moves (auto-rebase or merge-queue needed for autonomous loops)","status":"open","type":"feature","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-05T17:04:02.448Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-05T17:04:02.448Z","description":"When the base branch moves between run-PR open and auto-merge (e.g. tracker .seeds pushes, prompt fixes), the PR can go DIRTY/BLOCKED forever: auto-merge never fires, the conductor's tree-equality wait times out, and a human must update the branch. Observed live 2026-09-05: PR #28 stranded DIRTY after unrelated .seeds sync pushes; host-side manual repair (merge base into run branch, push) unblocked it and the dogfood-gate re-ran. Wanted: engine-side automatic run-branch PR updates when the base moves (merge base into the run branch, or a merge queue), so the autonomous line does not depend on control-function repairs. Basis: conductor pass 01M1S6MSV4, PR #28, repair commit a98db89f2.","labels":["engine","workflows"]}
